  "title": "packet-ethertype: remove magic ethertype values",
  "description": "In the section handling Cisco ACI gleaning, the ethertype was being set\nto a raw magic value. In particular, the ethertype for IPv6 was\nbeing given as 0x86BB when its actual ethertype is 0x86DD. Replace these\nmagic bytes with `ETHERTYPE_FOO` defines from `epan/etypes.h`.\n\nIf there is some reason why the ethertype specified here for IPv6 must be different than the actual assigned ethertype for IPv6, we should still use `ETHERTYPE_FOO` for the others, and add a comment for *why* we aren't doing it for IPv6.",
